WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.172
We hurried out into the inn's courtyard.

2
00:00:17.693 --> 00:00:23.097
Holmes was quite excited and exclaimed, "By heavens, Watson, I think I've got it.

3
00:00:23.658 --> 00:00:25.920
Do you remember all those cow tracks we saw today?"

4
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.242
"Yes," I answered, perplexed.

5
00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:29.523
"They were everywhere."

6
00:00:30.303 --> 00:00:33.197
"Exactly. How many cows did you see on the moor today?"

7
00:00:33.937 --> 00:00:34.938
Holmes asked, smiling.

8
00:00:34.958 --> 00:00:37.719
"None," I said, not understanding.

9
00:00:38.599 --> 00:00:40.020
"Doesn't this seem strange?"

10
00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.360
continued Holmes.

11
00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:43.841
"Yes," I agreed.

12
00:00:44.802 --> 00:00:49.444
"Think about those tracks for a moment, Watson," said Holmes as he began to draw in the dirt.

13
00:00:50.344 --> 00:00:57.887
"Some looked like this: others like this: and occasionally like this: What does this suggest to you?"

14
00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:02.969
I shook my head and said, "Nothing, but I believe it means something to you."

15
00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:06.530
"Indeed," said Holmes.

16
00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:13.252
"The cow must be quite remarkable because it can walk, canter and gallop, and I have never met

17
00:01:13.292 --> 00:01:14.052
a cow like that."

18
00:01:14.892 --> 00:01:16.913
Holmes and I slipped into the stable unnoticed.

19
00:01:17.553 --> 00:01:20.513
Holmes immediately went to the horses and raised one of their legs.

20
00:01:21.094 --> 00:01:26.415
Holmes laughed out loud and said, "The horses have old horseshoes, but they have been put on very

21
00:01:26.495 --> 00:01:32.822
recently." I wanted to ask Holmes to explain, but before I could, an extremely angry Mr.

22
00:01:32.882 --> 00:01:36.145
Hayes burst into the stable holding a short, metal-headed stick.

23
00:01:36.905 --> 00:01:39.447
"Spies! What are you doing here!"

24
00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:40.728
he screamed.

25
00:01:41.548 --> 00:01:45.711
I was glad that I had my revolver in my pocket, because he walked toward us with murder

26
00:01:45.751 --> 00:01:46.312
in his eyes.

27
00:01:46.332 --> 00:01:48.113
"Why, Mr.

28
00:01:48.193 --> 00:01:50.154
Hayes," said Holmes coolly.

29
00:01:50.174 --> 00:01:52.516
"You act as if you have something to hide."

30
00:01:53.317 --> 00:02:00.100
The man mastered his emotions with a supreme effort of will, and said with a fake laugh, "Poke

31
00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:02.821
around as you like, you will find nothing here.

32
00:02:03.861 --> 00:02:06.242
Once you've had a look, you had better leave at once."

33
00:02:07.082 --> 00:02:08.942
"We've had a look," said Holmes.

34
00:02:08.963 --> 00:02:10.883
"And my ankle is feeling better.

35
00:02:11.423 --> 00:02:13.064
Perhaps we'll walk back to the Hall."

36
00:02:13.084 --> 00:02:16.264
"The road's over there," said Mr.

37
00:02:16.324 --> 00:02:17.945
Hayes, waving his menacing stick.

38
00:02:18.645 --> 00:02:19.785
The man watched us leave.

39
00:02:20.105 --> 00:02:23.987
We had walked along the road for only about five minutes when Holmes suddenly stopped.

40
00:02:24.627 --> 00:02:27.247
"I think we need to return to the inn," said Holmes.

41
00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:29.188
"There's one more piece to this puzzle.

42
00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.401
I need to find it before we see the duke."

43
00:02:32.661 --> 00:02:35.162
I looked at Holmes and said, "That Mr.

44
00:02:35.202 --> 00:02:36.022
Hayes is a villain.

45
00:02:36.282 --> 00:02:36.922
I'm sure of it."

46
00:02:37.702 --> 00:02:38.422
"Watson! Quick!

47
00:02:38.762 --> 00:02:39.343
Off the road!"

48
00:02:39.843 --> 00:02:40.903
whispered Holmes urgently.

49
00:02:41.563 --> 00:02:46.365
A cyclist was coming quickly down the road from Holdernesse Hall, and Holmes and I had only a

50
00:02:46.405 --> 00:02:47.485
moment to hide ourselves.

51
00:02:48.125 --> 00:02:50.606
We watched as the cyclist passed in a cloud of dust.

52
00:02:51.146 --> 00:02:56.047
When he had passed I let out a soft whistle and Holmes exclaimed, "It was Mr.

53
00:02:56.087 --> 00:02:59.048
Wilder, the duke's secretary; our plot thickens.

54
00:02:59.616 --> 00:03:01.157
Come! Let us return to the inn."

55
00:03:02.198 --> 00:03:05.321
As night fell, we carefully made our way back to the inn, and hid.

56
00:03:06.001 --> 00:03:07.463
The courtyard appeared deserted.

57
00:03:07.943 --> 00:03:12.967
Wilder's bicycle rested against the wall, but we could hear sounds coming from the stable.

58
00:03:13.648 --> 00:03:17.471
A moment later we heard the clatter of hooves and the rattle of a cart moving at a

59
00:03:17.551 --> 00:03:18.291
furious pace.

60
00:03:18.311 --> 00:03:20.733
"What do you make of that?"

61
00:03:21.214 --> 00:03:21.834
I asked Holmes.

62
00:03:21.854 --> 00:03:25.197
"One man fleeing in a cart," replied Holmes.

63
00:03:25.217 --> 00:03:26.438
"But it wasn't Mr.

64
00:03:26.458 --> 00:03:28.560
Wilder, because there he is at the window.

65
00:03:29.044 --> 00:03:30.545
He seems to be expecting someone."

66
00:03:31.305 --> 00:03:35.647
A second figure appeared on the road five minutes later, and the secretary opened the door.

67
00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:38.208
"Curious," said Holmes.

68
00:03:39.028 --> 00:03:40.809
"Come, we must have a look into the inn."

69
00:03:41.669 --> 00:03:44.331
Holmes used my back to climb up and peek in the window.

70
00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:46.852
He was hardly up before he was down again.

71
00:03:46.872 --> 00:03:48.212
"Come, my friend.

72
00:03:48.532 --> 00:03:49.593
Our work is nearly done.

73
00:03:50.053 --> 00:03:51.414
We need to get back to the school.

74
00:03:51.994 --> 00:03:54.735
I think by tomorrow evening we'll be returning to London."

75
00:03:55.415 --> 00:04:00.190
When I awoke the following morning, Holmes was gone, so I occupied myself with the newspaper.

76
00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:05.593
Holmes returned by mid-morning, and said, "It's time for us to pay a visit to Holdernesse Hall."

77
00:04:07.174 --> 00:04:09.935
On our arrival we were greeted by a very nervous Mr.

78
00:04:09.976 --> 00:04:12.737
Wilder, who was obviously not pleased to see us.

79
00:04:13.658 --> 00:04:16.719
"If you have come to see the duke, I am afraid it will have to wait.

80
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:17.780
The duke is sick."

81
00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.782
"Sick or not, I will see the duke!"

82
00:04:21.282 --> 00:04:24.284
insisted Holmes, who simply would not accept no for an answer.

83
00:04:24.936 --> 00:04:25.797
An hour later, Mr.

84
00:04:25.837 --> 00:04:27.478
Wilder led us into the duke's study.

85
00:04:27.498 --> 00:04:34.221
"Your Grace," said Holmes formally, "I believe my business with you should be conducted in the absence of

86
00:04:34.242 --> 00:04:34.982
your secretary."

87
00:04:35.983 --> 00:04:40.545
Mr. Wilder turned very pale, and appeared about to protest when the duke dismissed him.

88
00:04:41.806 --> 00:04:42.286
After Mr.

89
00:04:42.306 --> 00:04:47.029
Wilder had left, Holmes asked, "Is it true you offered a reward for this case?"

90
00:04:47.549 --> 00:04:48.330
The duke nodded.

91
00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:56.610
Holmes continued, "Ten thousand pounds—five for anyone who could name the whereabouts of your son, and another five

92
00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:58.170
for the names of the people involved."

93
00:04:58.951 --> 00:04:59.831
Again the duke nodded.

94
00:04:59.851 --> 00:05:01.812
"Excellent," said Holmes.

95
00:05:02.232 --> 00:05:04.573
"Please write me a check for ten thousand pounds."

96
00:05:05.413 --> 00:05:07.194
The duke stood up and glared at Holmes.

97
00:05:07.214 --> 00:05:09.155
"Is this a joke?"

98
00:05:10.235 --> 00:05:12.336
"Not at all, Your Grace," said Holmes.

99
00:05:13.017 --> 00:05:19.159
"Your son is at the Fighting Cock Inn, and "And and who do you accuse?"

100
00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:20.880
interrupted the anxious duke.

101
00:05:21.836 --> 00:05:24.438
"I accuse YOU," said Holmes firmly.

102
00:05:25.038 --> 00:05:27.420
The duke sat down with his head down and wrote the check.

103
00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:33.745
"I will make the check out for 12,000 pounds," said the duke, "if you will kindly forget this

104
00:05:33.805 --> 00:05:34.545
whole incident."

105
00:05:35.366 --> 00:05:36.286
Holmes shook his head.

106
00:05:36.306 --> 00:05:41.450
"Too late for that, Your Grace, the murderer of the schoolteacher has already been arrested."

107
00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:43.872
"I see," said the duke.

108
00:05:44.432 --> 00:05:46.273
"Then it is time for a complete confession."

109
00:05:47.014 --> 00:05:48.215
The duke explained how Mr.

110
00:05:48.255 --> 00:05:52.009
Wilder was his illegitimate son, and how he was jealous of the young lord.

111
00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:56.692
The young lord had been sent to the Priory School for fear of his safety.

112
00:05:57.532 --> 00:06:02.515
Mr. Wilder kidnapped the young lord in order to blackmail the duke, but the German teacher had seen

113
00:06:02.535 --> 00:06:02.975
them leave.

114
00:06:03.675 --> 00:06:08.418
Mr. Wilder and the young lord had left the school in a cart, driven by the innkeeper.

115
00:06:09.158 --> 00:06:10.579
The German teacher had followed them.

116
00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:15.322
The innkeeper, worried about getting caught, had hit the schoolteacher with his club.

117
00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:18.984
Unfortunately the German teacher had died from his injuries.

118
00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:24.475
Holmes and I had not spotted the hooves of the horse and carriage because the innkeeper had cleverly

119
00:06:24.555 --> 00:06:27.436
changed the horseshoes, and made them look like cows' hooves.

120
00:06:28.237 --> 00:06:31.419
Holmes scolded the duke, and the duke accepted the scolding quietly.

121
00:06:32.219 --> 00:06:39.283
That evening as Holmes and I boarded our London-bound train, Holmes chuckled and said, "A most satisfactory ending

122
00:06:39.443 --> 00:06:40.904
to a sordid family affair.

123
00:06:41.744 --> 00:06:46.387
I believe our duke will be a much better father to both sons, and we, my dear friend,

124
00:06:46.867 --> 00:06:48.088
are a great deal richer."
